<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Del Monte lifts year earnings, div.</title>
<headline>Del Monte lifts year earnings, div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Nov 30 (million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Headline shr, attrib (cts)  50.1  vs 42.2</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 19.0	  vs 16.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had expected Delfood to report earnings per share of 52 cents with the dividend hiked to 19-22 cents.  </p>
<p>    Earnings/share (cts)  44.5	  vs 42.6</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   152.35	vs 145.54</p>
<p>    Exceptionals	    19.065	vs 1.26</p>
<p>    Headline earnings     171.42	vs 144.28</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   215.57	vs 142.60</p>
<p>    Tax			 6.45	  vs 0.31</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   111.65	vs 54.10</p>
<p>    Turnover		  3,301.15    vs 1,837.93</p>
<p>Div payable March 27</p>
<p>on register March 7</p>
<p>Full name: Del Monte Royal Foods Ltds</p>
<p>    Share of associates'  56.73	 vs 3.10</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
